## 1. Track 2 Clean-Room Reverse Engineering & Protocol Recovery (NabilRFG12/Reverse-Engineer-anything)

When assimilating closed, binary-only, or AGPL/copyleft-licensed toolchains under Track 2 (Clean-Room Synthesis):
- **Autonomous Disassembly & AST Inversion**: Use headless decompiler pipelines (e.g. Ghidra/BinaryNinja/Radare2 MCP bridges) to recover structural data types and control flows without copying source code.
- **Protocol & Network Sniffing Isolation**: Trace RPC / WebSocket wire protocols to extract declarative schema contracts (JSON Schema / Protobuf specs) rather than relying on bundled client libraries.
- **Clean-Room Boundary**: Team A (Auditor / RE agent) inspects the compiled artifact and writes architectural specifications and black-box test suites; Team B (Builder agent) implements clean TypeScript/Python modules strictly against the extracted interface specifications.

## 2. Generative Media & 3D Engine Agent Skills (scenario-labs/skills)

Architectural patterns for integrating agentic 3D/2D game asset and texture pipelines:
- **Pre-Cost Execution Gate**: Mandate cost calculation and budget checks before triggering external cloud rendering / model inference endpoints to prevent credit exhaustion.
- **Brand & Character Consistency Locks**: Maintain deterministic seed anchors and reference image embeddings across generative pipelines to ensure persistent visual identity across frames/assets.
- **Headless DCC Tool Automation**: Expose standardized MCP tool interfaces for Blender, Unreal Engine, and Unity so agents can run headless script batches (e.g. UV unwrapping, mesh decimation, texture baking) via CLI.

## 3. High-Velocity Fullstack Compilers & Edge Bundling (farming-labs/farm.js)

Patterns for zero-latency UI iteration and multi-target deployments:
- **Renderer-Agnostic Core**: Decouple JSX/React compilation from the underlying runtime (Node.js, Nitro, Bun, Cloudflare Workers, Edge).
- **Sub-Second HMR & AOT Compilation**: Employ Ahead-of-Time AST analysis to identify static DOM trees and compile Server Actions with typed RPC stubs automatically.
- **Zero-Config Rust/TS Hybrid Architecture**: Leverage native binary cores for heavy file-watching and module graph resolution while exposing standard Vite-compatible plugin hooks.

## 4. Headless Chrome CDP REA Protocol & Dual WebGL/2D Canvas Stabilization (morluto/rea & ui-reverse-engineer)

When running zero-token local reverse-engineering, visual state audits, and DOM extraction via Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP):
- **Isolated User Data Directory**: Always launch Chrome with `--user-data-dir=$(mktemp -d)` to prevent macOS sandbox / permission collisions (`DevToolsActivePort: Operation not permitted`) against default user profiles.
- **CDP Page Target Selection Filtering**: Under modern Chrome (130+), querying `/json` or `/json/list` returns internal browser surfaces (e.g. `chrome://omnibox-popup.top-chrome/`) as `type: "page"`. Never connect blindly to `targets[0]`. Always filter targets where `target.type == "page"` AND `target.url.startswith("http")` (or matching application origin).
- **Unhandled WebGL Exception Guard & 2D CAD Fallback**: `new THREE.WebGLRenderer()` throws an unhandled error in headless environments without hardware acceleration or when context creation fails. An unhandled exception during `DOMContentLoaded` completely halts the JavaScript event loop, terminating all subsequent 2D drafting, catalog hydration, and UI interactions. Wrap WebGL initialization in `try...catch` and trigger an automated fallback to full-featured 2D CAD mode.
- **Hidden Canvas Layout Collapse**: Canvases initialized inside hidden tabs (`display: none` / Tailwind `.hidden`) yield `0x0` dimensions or fall back to browser default `300x150`. Ensure an explicit `resizeCADCanvas()` hook recalculates bounds using `getBoundingClientRect()` or viewport fallbacks with HiDPI scaling whenever switching views.

